  "theorem": "On the normalized lowest Fourier carrier, vertex relative information has radial terms through degree eleven and first phase-dependent term +(7776/11) r^12 cos(12 phi). Thus a canonical information functional supplies the form and sign of the first D12 anisotropy. In the declared negative-feedback model V_g=I-(g/2)<q,Aq>, the uniform state loses local stability exactly when g>12/lambda_1. Positive information coupling, and in particular unit coupling, does not create a nonzero radius. The strict operator alone supplies neither a rule choosing g above threshold nor one realized phase.",
